# Project: Quran Kids Arabic Pronunciation App
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

## Architecture Overview

This is a monorepo with three parts:
- **mobile/** — React Native / Expo 54 app (TypeScript, Zustand, expo-router, Vitest)
- **backend/** — Python FastAPI ASR service (`asr_app.py`, wav2vec2-large-xlsr-53-arabic)
- **docs/** — Product requirements and research notes (German language)

## Tech Stack

| Layer    | Stack                                                        |
|----------|--------------------------------------------------------------|
| Mobile   | React Native 0.81, Expo 54, expo-router 6, Zustand 4, Vitest 4 |
| Backend  | Python 3.12, FastAPI, wav2vec2 (Grosman XLSR-53 Arabic), torchaudio |
| Testing  | Vitest (mobile), pytest (backend)                            |
| Styling  | Inline styles / React Native StyleSheet (no CSS-in-JS lib)  |

## Key Conventions

- Mobile source lives in `mobile/src/` (components, store, lib, data, hooks)
- App routes are in `mobile/app/` using expo-router file-based routing
- State management: Zustand stores in `mobile/src/store/`
- Tests: colocated `.test.ts` files next to source
- Backend: single file `backend/asr_app.py` (FastAPI)
- Docs are in German
- All Arabic text must handle RTL correctly

## Commands

| Task                | Command                          | Working Dir |
|---------------------|----------------------------------|-------------|
| Run mobile          | `npx expo start`                 | mobile/     |
| Run tests (mobile)  | `npm run test` or `vitest run`   | mobile/     |
| Run backend         | `uvicorn asr_app:app --reload`   | backend/    |
| Lint mobile         | `npm run lint`                   | mobile/     |

## Important Files (read these before making changes)

- `docs/mobile-kinder-app-anforderungen.md` — Full product requirements
- `docs/backend-cpu-migration-und-scoring.md` — Backend architecture decisions
- `mobile/src/store/` — All state logic
- `backend/asr_app.py` — ASR scoring pipeline

## Do NOT

- Add new state management libraries (use Zustand)
- Add CSS-in-JS libraries
- Modify `.env.local` files
- Add dependencies without explicit user approval
- Re-read large files like notebooks (.ipynb) — they are research artifacts

## Token-Saving Instructions for AI Assistants

- Prefer targeted file reads over full-directory scans
- Never read `node_modules/`, `.venv/`, `dist/`, `.expo/`, or `.ipynb` files
- When editing, use precise small diffs — avoid rewriting entire files
- Reference this file for architecture questions instead of re-exploring
- For mobile work: start with `mobile/src/store/` and `mobile/app/`
- For backend work: start with `backend/asr_app.py`
